My reading of this is that the surface order of sumti doesn't matter, whereas
the presence or absence of a "se" conversion does matter.  This is precisely
the notion you say "would be really confusing, and [you] don't see the point
of it" in response to Lojbab.  Now admittedly,

> Esperanto certainly does not claim to reflect predicate logic.

but what's sauce for one might well have some piquancy for the other, no?

